# Source preparation pipeline to be run from mapterhorn/pipelines folder.
#
# National-scope sea/ocean fallback for the JCI 2026-09 effort (see
# mapterhorn-japan-bridge's HANDOVER.md/DECISIONS.md). Successor to the
# small Hakodate-area `jphakodatetrialsea` pilot (D11) that proved the
# mechanism -- see that decision's investigation for why GLO-30 (not a
# separate bathymetry source) is the right choice: upstream mapterhorn's
# own published data uses GLO-30 as its universal land+sea fallback too
# (confirmed by reading upstream's source-catalog directly), and GLO-30
# reports near-0m for open water, verified non-corrupt across all zoom
# levels in the pilot.
#
# 275 of `source-catalog/glo30`'s 24,674 global 1x1-degree tiles,
# filtered to a generous rectangular bounding box (lat 20-46N, lon
# 122-154E) rather than a precise EEZ polygon -- chosen because GLO-30's
# own tile inventory already appears to exclude pure-open-ocean tiles
# with no land content (24,674/64,800 possible global cells is
# consistent with land+coastal-adjacent coverage only, not literally
# every ocean cell), so a precise EEZ polygon filter would likely
# produce nearly the same result as this simpler rectangle for any
# genuinely deep-ocean gap -- not worth the added complexity here.
#
# Verified this rectangle's real tile coverage (2026-08-19) against
# every territory Hidenori asked about, by direct coordinate lookup in
# glo30/file_list.txt (not just "the bounding box theoretically
# contains this point" -- confirmed a real tile exists there):
# Northern Territories (Habomai/Shikotan/Kunashiri/Etorofu, up to
# Etorofu's NE tip ~45.5N/148.85E), Minamitorishima (24.28N/153.98E),
# Okinotorishima (20.42N/136.08E), Takeshima (37.24N/131.87E), Senkaku
# Islands (Uotsuri/Kuba, ~25.75-25.93N/123.47-123.68E), Yonaguni
# (24.45N/123.0E), Hateruma (24.06N/123.8E). All present.
#
# Like jphakodatetrialsea, this is a low-priority fallback: maxzoom is
# computed dynamically per-tile (aggregation_covering.py's
# get_smallest_overzoom), and GLO-30's real ~30m resolution computes to
# roughly z9-13 depending on latitude (see that script's own comments:
# S79->9, N66->10, N50->11, N49->12) -- always well below the 1m
# sources' z16, so it can never win their equal-maxzoom priority
# tie-break (D8) and never gets built up to a wastefully high zoom
# either; downsampling only ever builds *down* from each tile's own
# computed maxzoom, never up to match a neighboring higher-res source.
#
# Explicitly deferred/low-priority per Hidenori (2026-08-19): this
# entry is prepared but not yet downloaded -- the core aalto GeoTIFF
# DEM upload work takes precedence over starting this download.
[no-cd]
default:
    uv run python source_download.py jpnationalsea
    uv run python source_bounds.py jpnationalsea
    uv run python source_polygonize.py jpnationalsea 4
